WEBVTT

00:00:00.750 --> 00:00:05.800
The first match of FFI Vision 2's Asia preliminaries!

00:00:05.800 --> 00:00:08.110
Inazuma Japan narrowly manages to win!

00:00:08.770 --> 00:00:14.570
Nevertheless, will these members who are close to amateurs really be able to get through the district preliminaries?

00:00:14.570 --> 00:00:18.300
Why do you think Coach Kuroiwa chose our members?

00:00:19.550 --> 00:00:23.410
Whatever his reason, there's only one thing that this team is in desperate need of right now.

00:02:04.920 --> 00:02:11.120
Since all of you here, besides the three of us, are beginners at soccer, I'm sure that you're uncertain on what to do with yourselves.

00:02:11.120 --> 00:02:15.400
But if you keep working on basic training, you're sure to get better.

00:02:15.400 --> 00:02:17.150
Let's do our best together!

00:02:23.520 --> 00:02:28.050
<i>But none of us are here because we wanted to play soccer.</i>

00:02:28.050 --> 00:02:32.000
<i>Each of us was hired under certain terms.</i>

00:02:33.200 --> 00:02:36.970
Even so, everyone fought to win the first match.

00:02:36.970 --> 00:02:40.220
It'll be fine. I'm sure it will all be fine.

00:02:48.250 --> 00:02:49.600
Where are the others?

00:02:50.100 --> 00:02:52.560
I think it has to do with the terms of our contract.

00:02:53.200 --> 00:02:54.600
Terms?

00:02:54.600 --> 00:03:00.750
Yeah. Attending practice until we won the first match was mandatory.

00:03:00.750 --> 00:03:03.670
But after that, we're free to do whatever we want until the next game.

00:03:03.670 --> 00:03:04.330
What?

00:03:04.820 --> 00:03:05.400
Oh no...

00:03:06.400 --> 00:03:08.570
Who made that decision?

00:03:08.570 --> 00:03:09.960
Me.

00:03:10.600 --> 00:03:12.300
Coach Kuroiwa!

00:03:12.300 --> 00:03:15.200
Why? Why would you make an agreement like that?

00:03:15.200 --> 00:03:17.470
Captain, begin practice.

00:03:18.700 --> 00:03:21.320
But not everyone is here yet.

00:03:21.320 --> 00:03:23.420
There is no need to wait for them.

00:03:24.170 --> 00:03:25.370
Yes, sir...

00:03:25.370 --> 00:03:26.170
What is the practice menu?

00:03:27.170 --> 00:03:29.020
That is for you to decide.

00:03:33.770 --> 00:03:36.500
He lets a situation like this happen freely?

00:03:36.950 --> 00:03:39.350
Is this what a coach should be doing?

00:03:39.350 --> 00:03:42.770
He really is hard to understand.

00:03:42.770 --> 00:03:43.920
Nozaki-san.

00:03:43.920 --> 00:03:45.650
Call me Sakura.

00:03:45.650 --> 00:03:49.120
Now that I think about it, some people didn't show up either back when I was in rhythmic gymnastics.

00:03:50.520 --> 00:03:51.520
I'll go get the others.

00:03:53.320 --> 00:03:56.350
Hey, let's just start practice on our own.

00:03:56.350 --> 00:03:58.220
B-But...

00:03:58.220 --> 00:04:00.550
Even Coach Kuroiwa said he was okay with that.

00:04:00.550 --> 00:04:01.720
But still...

00:04:01.720 --> 00:04:03.000
I'll go.

00:04:03.770 --> 00:04:06.070
I'll go get the others.

00:04:06.070 --> 00:04:07.500
You guys start practicing first.

00:04:07.800 --> 00:04:09.850
Thanks, Aoi!

00:04:09.850 --> 00:04:12.300
We should be training with people who actually want to be here.

00:04:12.300 --> 00:04:14.150
Right, Shindou-san?

00:04:14.150 --> 00:04:15.020
You too, Tsurugi-kun!

00:04:16.100 --> 00:04:16.900
Sure...

00:04:21.770 --> 00:04:23.870
Ibuki-kun, are you in?

00:04:25.170 --> 00:04:26.500
I'm opening the door.

00:04:34.770 --> 00:04:37.540
Speaking of which, you use balls in rhythmic gymnastics too, don't you?

00:04:37.750 --> 00:04:39.850
Yep, like this!

00:04:43.100 --> 00:04:43.950
Wow!

00:04:45.150 --> 00:04:46.720
I've heard of you.

00:04:46.720 --> 00:04:53.120
You're Asia's genius athlete who not only won the national championship but also medals in an official world-class tournament...

00:04:53.120 --> 00:04:54.180
Nozaki Sakura.

00:04:54.600 --> 00:04:55.700
You've heard of me?

00:04:55.700 --> 00:04:57.450
I'm so happy!

00:04:57.450 --> 00:05:04.400
Coach said that if I play in Inazuma Japan, I'll be able to study abroad in the world's best rhythmic gymnastics team.

00:05:05.620 --> 00:05:10.620
But from our last game, I guess I find soccer a bit fun.

00:05:11.200 --> 00:05:12.920
All right!

00:05:12.920 --> 00:05:16.620
Hearing you guys say that makes me really happy!

00:05:16.620 --> 00:05:21.210
Maybe you can use rhythmic gymnastic moves to come up with a hissatsu technique.

00:05:21.450 --> 00:05:23.300
That would be wonderful!

00:05:23.650 --> 00:05:27.500
Then, maybe something like this?

00:05:28.820 --> 00:05:32.250
It's pretty amazing how you can keep the ball stuck to you like that, but...

00:05:32.250 --> 00:05:33.620
It's a total foul...

00:05:35.170 --> 00:05:36.170
Oh, I see.

00:05:36.170 --> 00:05:38.550
You can't use your hands in soccer.

00:05:39.050 --> 00:05:41.970
Goalkeepers can, though.

00:05:41.970 --> 00:05:43.770
Then I want to try being goalkeeper!

00:05:44.420 --> 00:05:46.520
Uh, I guess we can try it out a little!

00:05:47.170 --> 00:05:51.120
Why didn't the rhythmic gymnastics association stop Nozaki from joining this team?

00:05:51.120 --> 00:05:56.080
She's a talented, experienced athlete with a promising future ahead of her, so why...?

00:05:57.100 --> 00:05:58.000
Come on!

00:05:58.650 --> 00:05:59.600
Here I go.

00:06:01.570 --> 00:06:03.600
I can't do it!

00:06:06.220 --> 00:06:10.020
That shoot came so fast! It's too scary...

00:06:10.020 --> 00:06:11.950
No goalkeeper position for you.

00:06:11.950 --> 00:06:13.100
I'm sorry.

00:06:13.520 --> 00:06:17.500
But you'll definitely be able to make use of that flexibility of yours in soccer, Sakura!

00:06:18.000 --> 00:06:20.520
Really? Then I'll do my best at soccer!

00:06:20.950 --> 00:06:22.600
Okay! Let's work hard together!

00:06:24.650 --> 00:06:28.450
I want to learn how to dribble without getting the ball stolen.

00:06:29.350 --> 00:06:31.270
Tenma's the dribbling expert.

00:06:31.270 --> 00:06:35.040
If you learn how to make short stepwork, it'll make you stronger against tackling.

00:06:35.570 --> 00:06:37.040
How do I do that?

00:06:37.820 --> 00:06:42.000
Why not try out an idea I came up with when I first practiced soccer, if you're okay with that?

00:06:42.750 --> 00:06:48.510
You do a zigzag dribble by moving left and right around the red-blue-red-blue.

00:06:49.120 --> 00:06:49.800
Okay!

00:06:54.470 --> 00:06:57.050
He's a fast runner, but...

00:06:57.050 --> 00:06:59.230
I wouldn't call that dribbling.

00:06:59.620 --> 00:07:01.820
Start off by making more precise moves.

00:07:01.820 --> 00:07:04.170
You can speed up after you've gotten used to it!

00:07:04.600 --> 00:07:06.320
O-Okay.

00:07:10.400 --> 00:07:13.020
That's it, Matatagi! Keep it up!

00:07:14.000 --> 00:07:16.220
Captain, teach me too.

00:07:16.220 --> 00:07:17.120
Okay, let's do it!

00:07:20.920 --> 00:07:27.370
It's true that Nozaki's flexibility and Matatagi's speed will be helpful to Inazuma Japan.

00:07:27.370 --> 00:07:30.260
But the problem is whether or not they'll make it in time for the next match.

00:07:30.850 --> 00:07:33.650
I'll be constantly available to help them with practice!

00:07:33.650 --> 00:07:35.150
I'll help, too.

00:07:36.720 --> 00:07:40.060
Now if only the rest of the team will join us...

00:07:41.600 --> 00:07:42.190
Aoi!

00:07:42.720 --> 00:07:43.550
How did it go?

00:07:44.470 --> 00:07:45.750
Well...

00:07:46.270 --> 00:07:47.770
I'm opening the door.

00:07:58.070 --> 00:07:59.950
No one was in their rooms.

00:07:59.950 --> 00:08:02.750
It looks like they all left for different parts of this area.

00:08:17.900 --> 00:08:19.970
I'll show Shindou for looking down on me...

00:08:20.770 --> 00:08:22.480
I'll make him eat his words!

00:08:25.070 --> 00:08:28.020
The goal is just a little bigger than a basketball hoop.

00:08:28.370 --> 00:08:29.770
I can stop this!

00:08:38.850 --> 00:08:42.800
This is how strong I really am!

00:09:07.920 --> 00:09:09.650
Are you alone too?

00:09:11.120 --> 00:09:12.860
You're just like me.

00:09:22.150 --> 00:09:23.650
What the hell?

00:09:23.650 --> 00:09:25.120
You wanna go at us?

00:09:33.400 --> 00:09:35.300
You're waiting for someone...

00:09:35.300 --> 00:09:39.000
From your fancy bag and the conscious way you stand, you're on a date...

00:09:39.000 --> 00:09:40.550
No, make that a girls' night out.

00:09:41.150 --> 00:09:45.850
I don't think that colorful outfit was chosen with a boy in mind.

00:09:51.250 --> 00:09:53.900
There's nothing that gets past me.

00:09:55.170 --> 00:09:57.900
Added up makes it 10, subtracted makes it -8.

00:09:58.350 --> 00:10:03.250
Multiplied is 24, divided is 0.04166.

00:10:03.250 --> 00:10:06.200
Squared makes it 1,800,964.

00:10:09.670 --> 00:10:12.870
3 hours, 18 minutes, and 25 seconds until dinnertime.

00:10:12.870 --> 00:10:15.370
11,905 seconds.

00:10:15.370 --> 00:10:20.820
If I spend 85 minutes at the science museum and 60 minutes at the planetarium,

00:10:21.100 --> 00:10:25.520
how should I spend the rest of my 53 minutes and 25 seconds...?

00:10:28.720 --> 00:10:30.420
Hey, Tsurugi.

00:10:30.750 --> 00:10:31.270
Yes?

00:10:31.750 --> 00:10:36.450
Matatagi and Nozaki do possess high physical ability...

00:10:36.450 --> 00:10:38.600
But why is it them specifically?

00:10:38.600 --> 00:10:42.270
Perhaps they have something that sets them apart from other players with the same abilities as they do.

00:10:42.270 --> 00:10:46.580
Something that made them eligible to be chosen as representatives.

00:10:53.370 --> 00:10:55.220
Please!

00:10:55.220 --> 00:10:57.010
I want you to come to practice!

00:10:57.720 --> 00:10:59.350
You don't have to participate.

00:10:59.350 --> 00:11:00.420
You can just watch.

00:11:00.870 --> 00:11:02.930
Anyway, just come, okay?

00:11:05.920 --> 00:11:10.050
I've been thinking about those who didn't come today.

00:11:10.220 --> 00:11:16.520
None of them had any interest in soccer before now, so even though they're under a contract,

00:11:16.520 --> 00:11:20.620
maybe it's hard for them to play soccer when they don't even like it.

00:11:21.320 --> 00:11:22.110
Tenma...

00:11:22.700 --> 00:11:26.550
So, I want to provide them the opportunity to start liking it...

00:11:26.550 --> 00:11:31.580
Like how I started liking soccer after Gouenji-san saved me.

00:11:33.070 --> 00:11:35.750
Tenma is doing his best as Captain.

00:11:35.750 --> 00:11:38.770
I have to do the same as manager, too!

00:11:44.350 --> 00:11:48.270
In order to win the prelims, I'll need to level up myself too.

00:11:50.250 --> 00:11:50.810
Tsurugi!

00:11:54.700 --> 00:11:55.860
Ibuki.

00:11:56.650 --> 00:11:58.200
We need to talk.

00:11:59.150 --> 00:12:01.190
Additional members?

00:12:01.550 --> 00:12:02.550
Yes, sir.

00:12:02.550 --> 00:12:04.670
We only have eleven people right now.

00:12:04.670 --> 00:12:08.500
If even one of us got injured or involved in an accident, it will affect our game-

00:12:08.500 --> 00:12:09.970
I'll think about it.

00:12:10.970 --> 00:12:12.400
It should be done now!

00:12:13.750 --> 00:12:15.920
Is that all you wish to discuss with me?

00:12:18.200 --> 00:12:19.130
Yes, sir...

00:12:25.650 --> 00:12:28.400
Inazuma Eleven GO Galaxy!

00:12:30.700 --> 00:12:33.520
Inazuma Eleven GO Galaxy!

00:12:45.190 --> 00:12:46.160
Where's Tsurugi?

00:12:46.620 --> 00:12:50.700
He called Tenma earlier to say he wanted to practice alone today.

00:12:51.220 --> 00:12:52.320
I see.

00:12:52.320 --> 00:12:53.210
Shindou-san.

00:12:53.670 --> 00:12:56.990
Can I ask you to look over Matatagi and Sakura's training?

00:12:56.990 --> 00:12:58.070
What about you?

00:12:58.070 --> 00:12:59.650
I'll go talk with the others.

00:13:00.920 --> 00:13:02.020
Okay.

00:13:03.270 --> 00:13:06.440
Right when we need to be focusing on fighting the world...

00:13:07.120 --> 00:13:12.340
I ought to at least do something about these two, or else this team has no future.

00:13:12.340 --> 00:13:15.100
U-Um, sorry to get right down to it, but...

00:13:16.150 --> 00:13:19.020
Shindou-san, will you look over my training?

00:13:29.120 --> 00:13:31.770
Today in sports news!

00:13:31.770 --> 00:13:34.870
Our theme for today is "The future of New Inazuma Japan!"

00:13:35.370 --> 00:13:36.920
What do you say, sir?

00:13:36.920 --> 00:13:38.630
I don't see any chance for them.

00:13:39.120 --> 00:13:41.970
With the level they're at right now, winning the prelims is a far stretch for them.

00:13:42.370 --> 00:13:45.370
Do you also believe that Coach Kuroiwa is at fault for selecting unknown players-

00:13:45.720 --> 00:13:49.620
It's Sakura! Huh? Why is Sakura in Inazuma Japan?

00:13:49.620 --> 00:13:50.870
It can't be possible.

00:13:50.870 --> 00:13:53.220
In a way though, I guess this is a good thing?

00:13:53.220 --> 00:13:56.090
Now we won't have to practice with her anymore.

00:13:56.090 --> 00:13:57.490
When you put it that way...

00:13:57.490 --> 00:13:58.370
Yeah.

00:13:58.370 --> 00:14:01.860
I feel a little sorry for the people in Inazuma Japan who have to put up with her now, though.

00:14:13.070 --> 00:14:13.990
Tetsukado!

00:14:15.170 --> 00:14:18.960
I thought you might be here since I heard your dad is a fisherman.

00:14:19.590 --> 00:14:20.750
What do you want?

00:14:21.320 --> 00:14:23.170
I want you to come to practice.

00:14:23.170 --> 00:14:24.200
You can just watch.

00:14:24.670 --> 00:14:27.690
Sorry, but I'm not interested in soccer.

00:14:28.170 --> 00:14:31.320
You said you did boxing, right?

00:14:31.550 --> 00:14:32.180
Yeah.

00:14:32.570 --> 00:14:39.570
I bet it must be really fun, attacking with all sorts of punches and guarding with your arms, and using tactics against each other.

00:14:40.670 --> 00:14:46.720
Soccer is a team sport, but one-on-one defense/offense and tactics are important in it, too.

00:14:46.720 --> 00:14:50.950
If you try it just a little more, I'm sure you'll enjoy soccer just as much as boxing-

00:14:49.970 --> 00:14:50.950
Stop it!

00:14:51.520 --> 00:14:53.850
Don't you ever talk to me about boxing ever again!

00:15:01.590 --> 00:15:02.880
Tetsukado...

00:15:12.440 --> 00:15:14.300
I'm surprised you knew where to find me.

00:15:14.870 --> 00:15:17.310
When I asked people in town, they told me you would be here.

00:15:17.620 --> 00:15:20.300
Then you've also heard what they say about me.

00:15:21.270 --> 00:15:22.310
Yeah.

00:15:23.090 --> 00:15:25.420
People in this town hate us.

00:15:25.420 --> 00:15:27.850
So, you shouldn't get too close.

00:15:28.240 --> 00:15:30.820
You've been chosen for Inazuma Japan.

00:15:30.820 --> 00:15:32.340
Let's play soccer together!

00:15:32.340 --> 00:15:34.070
I'm sure you'll find it fun!

00:15:35.340 --> 00:15:39.150
Thanks for the invite, but honestly, I wish you'd leave me alone.

00:15:40.270 --> 00:15:41.570
Kusaka...

00:15:43.500 --> 00:15:46.090
Konoha, why don't you come with me to practice?

00:15:46.720 --> 00:15:51.170
It won't matter if I'm there or not.

00:15:51.890 --> 00:15:55.270
Soccer can be fully analyzed through calculations.

00:15:55.270 --> 00:15:58.600
I have no interest in something that I can easily calculate without me even leaving this desk.

00:15:59.240 --> 00:16:04.050
If you can prove to me that it is more interesting than this formula, however, that would be a different story.

00:16:06.790 --> 00:16:11.690
I don't have an interest in soccer itself, but I enjoy observing people.

00:16:11.690 --> 00:16:14.320
How people think and what actions they take based on that thinking.

00:16:14.990 --> 00:16:19.320
Once you know that, you can solve any crime in the world.

00:16:19.320 --> 00:16:20.320
Isn't that wonderful?

00:16:20.740 --> 00:16:23.640
Minaho, I want you to come to practice.

00:16:23.640 --> 00:16:25.520
That won't be necessary.

00:16:25.920 --> 00:16:27.540
Humans have emotions.

00:16:28.390 --> 00:16:30.850
Soccer is played by said humans.

00:16:30.850 --> 00:16:33.050
Their emotions create openings that you can take advantage of.

00:16:33.050 --> 00:16:37.300
No matter how skilled they are as a player, once you grab that opening, you can steal the ball from them.

00:16:37.700 --> 00:16:40.520
In other words, technique isn't important.

00:16:40.520 --> 00:16:43.170
Training for it is unnecessary.

00:16:45.940 --> 00:16:49.140
Matsukaze Tenma appears to be troubled.

00:16:49.800 --> 00:16:55.450
What's more, you appear to be enjoying his suffering.

00:17:04.020 --> 00:17:04.920
That's it for today-

00:17:04.920 --> 00:17:05.920
Not yet!

00:17:06.440 --> 00:17:08.790
I'm not satisfied yet!

00:17:08.790 --> 00:17:09.120
Come on!

00:17:11.170 --> 00:17:14.800
You're the only one on this team with the most powerful shoot, right?

00:17:14.800 --> 00:17:17.550
It's not practice if I'm not stopping the strongest shoot we have!

00:17:18.270 --> 00:17:19.420
Okay then.

00:17:19.420 --> 00:17:20.510
I won't hold back.

00:17:21.470 --> 00:17:22.810
Just how I want it!

00:17:23.490 --> 00:17:26.750
I don't care about soccer or Inazuma Japan.

00:17:26.750 --> 00:17:29.870
I'll make Shindou recognize my ability!

00:17:37.720 --> 00:17:40.740
From the look on your face, I take it you weren't successful.

00:17:41.390 --> 00:17:42.770
For today.

00:17:43.020 --> 00:17:44.520
But I won't give up.

00:17:44.520 --> 00:17:45.920
I'll go again tomorrow.

00:17:45.920 --> 00:17:47.700
And the day after that, and the day after that.

00:17:48.640 --> 00:17:49.540
Cold!

00:17:50.240 --> 00:17:52.460
Do your best, Captain!

00:17:52.900 --> 00:17:54.200
See you tomorrow!

00:18:03.590 --> 00:18:05.870
Okay, I'll do my best!

00:18:05.870 --> 00:18:09.670
Until everyone becomes interested in soccer, I'll keep trying!

00:18:09.670 --> 00:18:11.400
There's no time for that.

00:18:14.740 --> 00:18:16.070
Coach Kuroiwa.

00:18:16.570 --> 00:18:19.020
Your second match in the prelims is in three days.

00:18:19.020 --> 00:18:20.770
Here is what you will be doing tomorrow.

00:18:27.420 --> 00:18:31.340
Coach Kuroiwa is leaving everything to us and not doing anything himself!

00:18:31.340 --> 00:18:37.050
Thinking that we can win the Asia prelims with only 11 members and no backup is insane!

00:18:38.320 --> 00:18:42.010
Shindou, I trust Coach Kuroiwa.

00:18:43.070 --> 00:18:44.010
No way...

00:18:44.750 --> 00:18:45.890
That is all.

00:18:50.870 --> 00:18:54.400
Chairman Gouenji! I just can't take this anymore!

00:18:54.820 --> 00:19:00.390
It was you, along with only a few other people, who nominated Kuroiwa for coach!

00:19:00.390 --> 00:19:03.120
Even to the extent of making enemies of everyone else who works in the association!

00:19:03.120 --> 00:19:07.870
It was due to your distinguished service in rebuilding the soccer world that your nomination was accepted.

00:19:08.190 --> 00:19:12.500
But now what's happened? Almost all of the members he has chosen are beginners at soccer!

00:19:12.500 --> 00:19:14.620
I can only assume that he's desecrating soccer!

00:19:15.470 --> 00:19:17.850
Just why in the world would you choose someone like him-

00:19:17.850 --> 00:19:20.220
I have no intentions of changing the coach.

00:19:20.450 --> 00:19:21.950
There is something wrong with you!!

00:19:22.870 --> 00:19:23.870
Why?

00:19:23.870 --> 00:19:26.390
Why is Gouenji-san defending someone like him?

00:19:26.390 --> 00:19:30.520
Did you think I wouldn't know who he really is?!

00:19:31.320 --> 00:19:32.970
I'm sure that you are aware as well.

00:19:33.740 --> 00:19:38.540
If you let him have power, he'll drown the world of soccer into darkness again.

00:19:38.540 --> 00:19:42.530
He's like a shadow that covers the light, like the embodiment of darkness itself!!

00:19:43.140 --> 00:19:45.350
That is why he must be Coach.

00:19:47.270 --> 00:19:51.500
Because he knows, in every detail, both the darkness and the light.

00:19:52.900 --> 00:19:54.240
It's so pretty!

00:19:54.240 --> 00:19:56.520
I never knew there was a place like this.

00:19:56.520 --> 00:19:59.570
I like to come here when I have a lot on my mind.

00:19:59.570 --> 00:20:02.820
This is the place that the person I respect the most introduced to me.

00:20:03.920 --> 00:20:05.350
Is he involved in soccer?

00:20:05.590 --> 00:20:06.290
Yeah.

00:20:06.290 --> 00:20:10.350
He's amazing, not only as both a soccer player and a Coach, but also as a human being.

00:20:11.400 --> 00:20:14.320
I want to grow up to be like him one day.

00:20:16.320 --> 00:20:19.800
What are you going to do with the others not coming to practice?

00:20:22.040 --> 00:20:25.030
Tomorrow... everyone will come.

00:20:30.770 --> 00:20:32.150
Hey, look.

00:20:32.150 --> 00:20:33.750
Are they doing something down there?

00:20:40.370 --> 00:20:41.070
Why?!

00:20:41.420 --> 00:20:43.300
Tenma, what did you say to them?

00:20:43.820 --> 00:20:48.300
I wrote everyone an e-mail, telling them that we're deciding who can drop out of the team.

00:20:49.720 --> 00:20:52.120
You made that up to get everyone to come here, right?

00:20:52.970 --> 00:20:54.890
It's what Coach told me to do.

00:20:55.290 --> 00:20:57.270
You're all here.

00:21:00.340 --> 00:21:04.110
In that case, we will now begin the withdrawal exam for Inazuma Japan.

00:21:05.070 --> 00:21:08.350
If you pass, I will allow you to withdraw from the team.

00:21:08.350 --> 00:21:11.620
Of course, I will also fulfill the terms of your contract.

00:21:12.670 --> 00:21:14.210
Coach... Are you serious?!

00:21:14.920 --> 00:21:16.970
But, can you imagine this?

00:21:16.970 --> 00:21:22.570
Once this exam is over, not one of you will desire to leave this team.

00:22:53.970 --> 00:22:55.520
The fateful PK match!

00:22:55.520 --> 00:22:57.980
Each of the members put their feelings into the kick!

00:22:58.190 --> 00:23:00.190
Make your shoot for the future!

00:23:00.190 --> 00:23:03.190
Next, Inazuma Japan's Withdrawal Exam!

00:23:03.190 --> 00:23:05.570
This is super-dimensional soccer!

00:23:15.190 --> 00:23:19.820
The Inazuma Eleven GO Galaxy's proverb today is...

00:23:22.290 --> 00:23:26.340
If you keep working on basic training, you're sure to get better!

00:23:26.340 --> 00:23:27.350
That's all!
